# Whitelisted vulnerability IDs for pip-audit in CI.
#
# Format: one ID per line. Anything after `#` on a line is a comment.
# Use this file ONLY for advisories where:
#   - the vulnerable code path is not reachable from our usage, OR
#   - an upstream fix is pending and we have a tracking issue.
#
# Each entry MUST be followed by a comment explaining WHY and pointing
# at a tracking issue / PR. An ignore without justification is a code
# smell — the reviewer should ask "what's the fix plan?".
#
# Example:
#   GHSA-xxxx-yyyy-zzzz  # not exposed via our API surface; tracked in #123

MAL-2026-4750  # OSV malicious-packages feed flag against fastapi 0.136.3 — no fix version published, the legitimate fastapi release is in use, advisory tracks a typosquatting incident not the upstream package. Re-evaluate when OSV publishes a fix or withdraws the advisory.
PYSEC-2026-1325  # Minerva timing attack on ECDSA P-256 signing in the `ecdsa` package. Not reachable here: `ecdsa` is an unused transitive dependency of python-jose, and this platform signs with RS256 (settings.jwt_algorithm) and HS256 (SSO state) — never ECDSA — so SigningKey.sign_digest() is never called. Verification is unaffected per the advisory, and upstream has declined to fix ("side channel attacks out of scope, no planned fix"). Revisit if we ever adopt ES256 or drop python-jose for PyJWT.
